  {"date": "2021-10-29", "venue": "MGM Grand Garden Arena", "city": "Las Vegas", "state": "NV", "gap": 15, "set": "1", "jamchart": true, "jam": "Punishing play, typical of the song, cools. Out, then, from the song's familiar closing refrain, Trey shapes his tone, his sound heavy as a stone, and offset by spaceage Page.  On-point (somewhat incendiary) Fish, Mike anchors what becomes an oozing, liquid event. Lazer-like, the band enters a jam that evokes Floyd inside the walls of a cave, with terrific lead Fish. Listen again and again - Trey is so inventive - as there is always something different to hear, or say.", "out": ">", "prev": "Olivia's Pool", "next": "Mike's Song", "nb": 1},
  {"date": "2022-04-22", "venue": "Madison Square Garden", "city": "New York", "state": "NY", "gap": 10, "set": "1", "jamchart": true, "jam": "An extended take on the usual outro drifts into a hypnotic haze which Trey cuts through with melodic leads, buoyed by ample synthesizer and \"Quadrophonic Toppling\" quotes.", "out": ">", "prev": "Army of One", "next": "Bathtub Gin", "nb": 1},
